/*  Makers and unmakers — the end of `Pass1Hoist` (named constructors, then destructors),
    `CheckConstructor` in `TypeChecker.Functions.cs` and `CheckUnmake` in `TypeChecker.Objects.cs`.

    ★ In the tree a maker is an ordinary `(BindStatement …)` whose place 6 names the type it makes,
    with that type as its return: `Bind making a point to origin` gives back `(ObjectType "point")`.
    So it is hoisted, called and checked as a function; only its registration is its own. An
    unmaker is `(UnmakerDeclaration "name" "type" [body] line column)`.

    ⚠ Both are gathered from EVERY statement, at any depth (`AstSearch.EveryStatement`), not only
    the hoistable ones — so `gather-kind` walks the whole tree.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// Every node of one kind, anywhere under `shape`, in the order they are written.
    Bind void to gather-kind, given (the node shape, the text wanted, the series of node found):
        If shape's kind is wanted, insert shape into found.
        For each inner in shape's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom", cast gather-kind on (inner, wanted, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The makers registered on each type, then the one unmaker each type may have.
    Bind void or failure to hoist-makers unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define binds as a series of node.
        Cast gather-kind on (program, "BindStatement", binds).
        Define type-order as a series of text.
        Define makers as a map from text to node.
        For each declaration in binds, repeat:
            Define made-type as cast field-of on (declaration, 6).
            If cast is-nothing on (made-type) is false:
                Define type-name as cast unquoted on (made-type).
                Define group as the entry for type-name in makers.
                If group is void:
                    Define fresh-group as cast listed.
                    In makers, the entry for type-name becomes fresh-group.
                    Insert type-name into type-order.
                    Cast fresh-group's add on (declaration).
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Cast group's add on (declaration).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each type-name in type-order, repeat:
            Define group as (the entry for type-name in makers but void is cast listed)'s children.
            If cast one's definition-of on (type-name) is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{type-name}' is not a defined object type — 'making a {type-name}' has no type to register on", "",
                    cast numeric on (cast field-of on (item 1 of group, 7)), "declare a maker for '{type-name}'",
                    "Define 'object {type-name}' before declaring makers for it, or check the spelling.")).
            Done.
            Define names as a map from text to fact.
            For each maker in group, repeat:
                Define maker-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (maker, 1)).
                If (the entry for maker-name in names) is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{type-name}' already has a maker named '{maker-name}'", "",
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (maker, 7)), "declare another maker named '{maker-name}' for '{type-name}'",
                        "Constructor names must be unique per type. Rename one of them.")).
                Done.
                In names, the entry for maker-name becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.

        Define unmakers as a series of node.
        Cast gather-kind on (program, "UnmakerDeclaration", unmakers).
        Define unmade as a map from text to node.
        Define unmade-order as a series of text.
        For each unmaker in unmakers, repeat:
            Define type-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (unmaker, 2)).
            If (the entry for type-name in unmade) is not void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{type-name}' already has an unmaker — 'Bind unmaking a {type-name}' appeared twice", "",
                    cast numeric on (cast field-of on (unmaker, 4)), "declare a second unmaker for '{type-name}'",
                    "Remove the duplicate. Each type has exactly one unmaker — one way to die.")).
            Done.
            In unmade, the entry for type-name becomes unmaker.
            Insert type-name into unmade-order.
        Done.
        For each type-name in unmade-order, repeat:
            If cast one's definition-of on (type-name) is void:
                Define unmaker as the entry for type-name in unmade.
                If unmaker is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{type-name}' is not a defined object type — 'unmaking a {type-name}' has no type to register on", "",
                        cast numeric on (cast field-of on (unmaker, 4)), "declare an unmaker for '{type-name}'",
                        "Define 'object {type-name}' before declaring an unmaker for it, or check the spelling.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// `CheckUnmake`: the body sees its object as `one`, takes nothing and gives nothing back — so a
    /// `return a failure` in it is already refused, as a value returned from a void body.
    Bind void or failure to check-unmaker unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define type-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)).
        Define at-row as cast numeric on (cast field-of on (statement, 4)).
        If cast one's definition-of on (type-name) is void:
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{type-name}' is not a defined object type", "",
                at-row, "declare an unmaker for '{type-name}'",
                "Define 'object {type-name}' before declaring an unmaker for it.")).
        Done.
        Cast one's check-member-body on (type-name, at-row, cast listed, at-row, false, cast nothing,
            cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
    Done.
Done.
